from pathlib import Path
import json,base64
P=Path(__file__).parent;m=json.loads((P/'motion-manifest.json').read_text());frames=json.loads((P/'frame-metadata.json').read_text())['frames']
b64=lambda n:'data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode((P/n).read_bytes()).decode()
images={f['pose']:b64(f['outputPNG']) for f in frames}
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>California Towhee — one backward hop</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;margin:24px;max-width:1200px;background:#eee9d9;color:#26362d}h1{font-size:24px}button,input{margin:6px}canvas,img{image-rendering:pixelated}canvas{background:#e5e0cd;border:1px solid #b7b39e}section{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px}.card{padding:10px;background:#e5e0cd}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px}.limits{max-width:1000px}#status{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}</style></head><body><h1>California Towhee: one backward ground hop</h1><p>Four new drawn body/leg poses + existing neutral. One native edit. No rigged standing-sprite hop, app binding, complete double-scratch or feeding claim.</p><p>One-shot travel is24world units backward while facing right. The neutral is78world units long; the proposed density is67/78output pixels per world unit. Playback ends at the landed root. <b>Replay explicitly resets.</b></p><button id="play">Play once / replay</button><button id="pause">Pause</button><label>Tick <input id="tick" type="range" min="0" max="28" value="0"></label><label><input id="contacts" type="checkbox" checked>Contact/root overlay</label><p id="status"></p><section><div class="card"><p>Yard-scale:1CSS pixel per world unit</p><canvas id="yard" width="360" height="180"></canvas></div><div class="card"><p>Same source playback,2x inspection</p><canvas id="zoom" width="360" height="180" style="width:720px;height:360px"></canvas></div></section><p class="limits">Root is stationary through neutral/crouch, then moves only in the8airborne ticks. Grounded frames share an actual toe-pixel boundary anchor at[55.5,76] and lowest alpha128 edge at76. Airborne feet are unplanted. This anchors one support proxy; changing individual toe silhouettes and exact anatomy still need independent review. Rasterized preview contact can round by about1screen pixel; numeric world support is exact.</p><p class="limits">All four new drawings use one call-wide1.17384370016 scale, then whole-canvas3/32export. No per-pose fit, foot warp or source repaint. Compression/settle are deliberately lower body poses. Source lengths span roughly73–78world units as tail/body projection changes. Closed wings throughout; tucked toes in airborne pose are visibly curled and should be checked in enlarged crops. One native beak crossed an atlas cell boundary; disjoint component extraction retains it without cutting.</p><p><a href="https://www.allaboutbirds.org/guide/California_Towhee/lifehistory">Cornell natural-history basis</a>: California Towhees hop backward during ground double-scratch foraging. Our clip is a single hop; timing and distance are designed product values, not measured species kinematics.</p><details open><summary>Separate source-pose preview; fixed canvas, one play</summary><img width="96" height="96" src="POSEAPNG"></details><img style="max-width:100%;height:auto" src="CONTACTS"><details><summary>Exact motion metadata</summary><pre>MOTIONTEXT</pre></details><script>const motion=MOTION;const urls=IMAGES;const canvas=document.getElementById('yard'),ctx=canvas.getContext('2d'),zoom=document.getElementById('zoom'),zctx=zoom.getContext('2d');let currentTick=0,playing=false,start=0,loaded={};const slider=document.getElementById('tick');function draw(t){currentTick=Math.max(0,Math.min(28,Math.floor(t)));slider.value=currentTick;const s=motion.trajectory.samples[currentTick],meta=motion.frames.find(f=>f.pose===s.pose),density=motion.presentation.outputPixelsPerWorldUnit,pivot=motion.presentation.pivotOutputXY;ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled=false;ctx.fillStyle='#e5e0cd';ctx.fillRect(0,0,360,180);ctx.strokeStyle='#838571';ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(0,130);ctx.lineTo(360,130);ctx.stroke();ctx.drawImage(loaded[s.pose],s.rootWorldXY[0]-pivot[0]/density,s.rootWorldXY[1]-pivot[1]/density,96/density,96/density);if(document.getElementById('contacts').checked){ctx.strokeStyle=s.planted?'#26734c':'#a75a18';const [x,y]=s.rootWorldXY;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(x-3,y);ctx.lineTo(x+3,y);ctx.moveTo(x,y-3);ctx.lineTo(x,y+3);ctx.stroke();if(s.planted){const a=meta.toeBoundarySupportAnchorOutputXY;const ax=x+(a[0]-pivot[0])/density,ay=y+(a[1]-pivot[1])/density;ctx.fillStyle='#008345';ctx.fillRect(ax-1,ay-1,2,2)}else{ctx.fillStyle='#a75a18';ctx.fillRect(x-1,s.lowestToeBoundaryWorldY-1,2,2)}}ctx.fillStyle='#28362d';ctx.font='12px system-ui';ctx.fillText('Start190 → landed166. Ground y130.',8,16);ctx.fillText(s.pose+' / '+(s.planted?'planted':'airborne'),8,167);zctx.imageSmoothingEnabled=false;zctx.clearRect(0,0,360,180);zctx.drawImage(canvas,0,0);document.getElementById('status').textContent=`Tick ${currentTick}/28 • ${s.pose} • root[${s.rootWorldXY.map(v=>v.toFixed(3)).join(',')}] • ${s.planted?'fixed root; support error '+s.supportBoundaryErrorWorldUnits.toFixed(3):'unplanted; toe clearance '+s.toeClearanceWorldUnits.toFixed(3)}world units`;return s}function raf(now){if(playing){const t=Math.floor((now-start)*30/1000);draw(t);if(t>=28)playing=false}requestAnimationFrame(raf)}document.getElementById('play').onclick=()=>{draw(0);start=performance.now();playing=true};document.getElementById('pause').onclick=()=>playing=false;slider.oninput=()=>{playing=false;draw(Number(slider.value))};document.getElementById('contacts').onchange=()=>draw(currentTick);window.TOWHEE_REVIEW={ready:false,seek:t=>{playing=false;return draw(t)},getState:()=>motion.trajectory.samples[currentTick],play:()=>document.getElementById('play').click(),pause:()=>playing=false,getPlaying:()=>playing,motion};Promise.all(Object.entries(urls).map(([name,url])=>new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{const im=new Image();im.onload=()=>{loaded[name]=im;resolve()};im.onerror=reject;im.src=url}))).then(()=>{window.TOWHEE_REVIEW.ready=true;draw(0);requestAnimationFrame(raf)});</script></body></html>'''
html=html.replace('POSEAPNG',b64('source-poses.apng')).replace('CONTACTS',b64('normal-size-and-feet-contact-sheet.png')).replace('MOTIONTEXT',json.dumps(m,indent=2)).replace('MOTION',json.dumps(m)).replace('IMAGES',json.dumps(images));(P/'review.html').write_text(html)
print('Viewer ready')
